369|For example, some people love|
370|speaking in front of an audience.|
371|Whereas others|
372|prefer to work quietly,|
373|in a calmer environment.|
374|Me, I like communicating,|
375|but I wouldn't want to spend|
376|my whole day on the phone.|i=telephone:le téléphone
377|And I like organising ideas|
378|and explaining things,|
379|but I also need|
380|moments of concentration.|
381|So our personality|
382|can give us clues|
383|about the type of work that suits us.|
384|Exactly.|
385|Some people like routine.|
386|Others prefer variety.|
387|And some like working in a team,|
388|while others are more efficient alone.|
389|No preference|
390|is automatically better than another.|
391|We simply have to learn|
392|to know ourselves better.|
393|Yes. And it's also important|B={"mode":"word","bg":"carnet","note":"= nos qualités et nos compétences particulières"}
394|to identify our strengths.|
395|"Strengths" are our qualities|
396|and our particular skills.|
397|Exactly. Some people are organised,|
398|others are creative|
399|or especially patient.|BE
400|And sometimes, we don't even notice|
401|our own qualities.|
402|Why?|e=question
403|Because some things seem easy to us.|
404|We imagine that everyone|
405|has the same abilities.|
406|That's true. For example, someone|
407|who can explain complex ideas clearly|
408|may think it's an ordinary skill.|
409|Whereas it's a real strength.|
410|A good way to discover your qualities|
411|is to notice|
412|what others often ask us for.|
413|For example, if my friends always ask me|
414|to organise the trips,|
415|maybe it's because I'm good|
416|at planning itineraries.|
417|And if your colleagues regularly ask you|
418|to proofread their texts,|
419|maybe you have a gift for writing.|
420|And if everyone asks me|
421|to choose the restaurants?|
422|Then you probably have a special talent|
423|for finding good places to eat!|i=repas:de bonnes adresses e=rire
424|Finally, a recognised skill!|e=rire
425|But be careful, our strengths|
426|don't necessarily have to become our job.|
427|Yes. They can simply help us|
428|better understand what we enjoy.|
429|Exactly. And sometimes we discover|
430|our talents through unexpected experiences.|
431|You know, my cousin had absolutely no idea|
432|what job to choose after her studies.|
433|Oh really? What fields interested her?|e=question
434|She liked languages,|
435|drawing and communication,|
436|but she struggled to choose a direction.|
437|And how did she find her path?|
438|She did an internship at a small company.|
439|She had to prepare presentations|
440|and explain complicated information|
441|in a simple way.|
442|And did she like it?|
443|Enormously.|
444|She realised she loved|
445|turning complex ideas|
446|into visual content that's easy to understand.|
447|Ah, that's an interesting skill.|e=idee
448|Today, she works|
449|in visual communication.|
450|But when she was a teenager,|
451|she didn't even really know this job existed.|
452|That shows you can't always|
453|choose a job before knowing it exists.|
454|Exactly. And sometimes our direction|
455|appears gradually through experience.|
456|That's why there's no need to panic|
457|when you don't know your ideal job yet.|
458|And yet many young people|
459|feel enormous pressure|
460|when choosing their studies.|i=etudes:leurs études
461|That's true. They're sometimes asked|
462|to imagine their career|
463|for the next ten years|
464|when they're only just starting|
465|to discover the working world.|
466|And not everyone moves at the same pace.|
467|Exactly.|
468|Some people find their path very early.|
469|Others need several experiences.|
470|And some change careers|
471|after ten or fifteen years of work.|
472|Absolutely.|
473|Our priorities can change over time.|
474|At twenty, you may seek adventure.|
475|Later, you may give|
476|more importance to stability.|
477|Or want a more flexible job|
478|to spend time with your family.|
479|And it's not necessarily a failure|
480|to change direction.|
481|No. It can simply mean|
482|you've learned more about yourself.|
483|You know, I think there's a problem|
484|with the expression "dream job".|
485|Which one?|e=question
486|It sometimes gives the impression|
487|that a perfect profession exists somewhere.|
488|An exciting, well-paid job,|
489|with amazing colleagues|
490|and no stress?|
491|Exactly! And of course,|
492|lots of holidays and free coffee!|i=cafe:du café gratuit e=rire
493|Mathieu, you're asking for an awful lot!|e=rire
494|I know. But it's a dream, after all!|
495|More seriously,|
496|I don't think a perfect job exists.|
497|Me neither.|
498|Even a job you love|
499|has its difficulties.|
500|There can be deadlines, responsibilities,|
501|repetitive tasks|
502|or very busy periods.|
503|So an ideal job may not be|
504|a job without problems.|
505|Exactly.|
506|It's perhaps rather a job|
507|whose positive sides match|
508|what matters to us,|
509|and whose difficulties stay acceptable.|
510|I like that definition.|e=coeur
511|It's much more realistic.|
512|And it reminds us we don't need|
513|to find a perfect profession|
514|to build a satisfying life.|
515|You know, some people like their job,|
516|but mostly find happiness|
517|in their hobbies|
518|and their personal relationships.|
519|And that's perfectly legitimate.|e=coeur
520|So our job doesn't need|
521|to represent our whole identity.|
522|Absolutely.|B={"mode":"steps","bg":"craie","title":"Changer de carrière","items":[{"text":"réfléchir à ce qui nous manque","at":2},{"text":"chercher des informations","at":6},{"text":"discuter avec des professionnels","at":7},{"text":"préparer son projet progressivement","at":9}]}
523|But if someone wants to change careers,|
524|they can start by thinking about|
525|what's missing in their current job.|
526|For example, more creativity,|
527|freedom or stability.|
528|Yes. Then they can look for information,|
529|talk with professionals|
530|and discover the skills needed.|
531|And prepare their project gradually,|
532|especially if they have financial responsibilities.|
533|Exactly.|
534|A career change|
535|doesn't have to be immediate.|BE
536|And even if you finally decide|
537|to stay in your current job,|
538|this reflection can help us|
539|better understand our needs.|
540|Absolutely.|
541|Now, I'd like to talk about|
542|a few very useful expressions|
543|for our listeners.|
544|Great idea!|e=idee
545|Because talking about your work|
546|and your career plans|
547|is a common topic|
548|in French conversations.|
549|For example, to ask|
550|someone's job, you can say:|
551|"What do you do for a living?"|
552|Or: "What field|
553|do you work in?"|
554|And to talk about your ambitions, you can say:|
555|"I'd like to work in tourism."|
556|Or: "My dream would be to become an architect."|
557|Exactly.|
558|And if you're not sure of your choice yet,|
559|you can say:|
560|"I'm still thinking about|
561|my career path."|
562|"Career guidance"|
563|is looking for a job|
564|or a field that suits us.|
565|Very good. Now, let's review|
566|some natural expressions.|
567|Let's start with "trouver sa voie".|B={"mode":"compare","bg":"liege","title":"trouver ou changer ?","left":{"head":"trouver sa voie","sub":"découvrir sa direction","items":[{"text":"une direction qui nous correspond","at":2},{"text":"« dans le design »","at":5}]},"right":{"head":"changer de voie","sub":"une nouvelle direction","items":[{"text":"dans ses études","at":8},{"text":"dans sa carrière","at":8}]}}
568|"Trouver sa voie" means discovering|
569|a professional or personal direction|
570|that suits us.|
571|For example: "After several experiences,|
572|she found her path in design."|
573|Second expression: "changer de voie".|
574|It means choosing a new direction,|
575|often in your studies or career.|
576|For example:|
577|"After a few years in sales,|
578|he decided to change direction."|BE
579|Third expression:|B={"mode":"word","bg":"carnet","note":"= se sentir bien, progresser, trouver de la satisfaction"}
580|"to flourish in your work".|
581|It means feeling good,|
582|growing and finding satisfaction|
583|in your professional activity.|
584|For example: "She flourishes in her job|
585|because she likes helping others."|BE
586|Fourth expression:|
587|"to have a sense of something".|
588|It describes an ability|
589|or a particular quality.|
590|For example: "He has a knack for organising."|
591|Or: "She's good with people."|
592|Fifth expression: "gagner sa vie".|
593|It means earning the money you need|
594|to live through your work.|
595|For example: "He'd like to earn a living|
596|doing photography."|
597|And our last expression:|
598|"se reconvertir".|
599|"Se reconvertir" means|
600|changing job or professional field|
601|after already working in another sector.|
602|For example:|
603|"After ten years in finance, she decided|
604|to retrain as a teacher."|
605|There you go, six very useful expressions|
606|to talk about work and the future.|
607|And now, let's see how to make|
608|some sentences sound more natural in French.|
609|Let's start with: "I want to be a doctor."|B={"mode":"transform","bg":"craie","title":"Plus naturel","from":"Je *veux être* médecin.","to":"J'*aimerais devenir* médecin.","fromTag":"direct","toTag":"naturel","label":"conditionnel + devenir","en":"I'd like to become a doctor.","changeAt":1}
610|You can say: "I'd like to become a doctor."|
611|Or: "My dream would be to practise medicine."|BE
612|Second sentence:|
613|"I don't know which job to choose."|
614|You can say: "I'm still looking for|
615|the job that suits me."|
616|Or: "I'm still thinking|
617|about my career path."|
618|Third sentence:|
619|"I want a job that makes me happy."|
620|You can say: "I'd like to find|
621|a job where I can flourish."|
622|Or: "I'm looking for a job|
623|that's meaningful to me."|
624|Fourth sentence: "I'm good with people."|
625|You can say: "I have good people skills."|
626|Or: "Human contact|
627|is one of my strengths."|
628|Fifth sentence:|
629|"I don't have enough experience."|
630|You can say: "I still lack|
631|experience in this field,|
632|but I'm ready to learn."|
633|Or: "I'd like to develop my skills|
634|before applying."|
635|And our last sentence:|
636|"I want to try another job."|
637|You can say: "I'd like to explore|
638|new career possibilities."|
639|Or: "I'm considering a career change,|
640|but I'd rather find out more|
641|before making a decision."|
642|Very good. These expressions let us|B={"mode":"match","bg":"liege","pairs":[["gagner sa vie","to earn a living"],["un stage","an internship"],["exigeant","demanding"],["trouver sa voie","to find your path"]],"reveal":2}
643|talk about our plans|
644|in a more precise and natural way.|
